plugin-hostd-protocol (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The vocabulary sorting pass: the probe words (outcomes, reasons, steps,
    signals) and the pin verdict and pool words are domains of this package
    (probe, pin) and protocol.h generates its lists from them; the parameter
    scales are read from omx-contract's domain param; GroupingReason and
    RETRY_REASONS of both clients are written from plugin-hostd's domain
    plugin-hostd/grouping; the shared verbs and host words are read from
    omx-clap's domains, under the new omx-clap names.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The backward-compatibility removal: the ERR_LV2_* spellings of the error
    words are gone from host-errors.h, and plan, plan_get and estimate answer
    with their one reply form only; their reply schemas require every word of
    it (#110). This removes API, hence a new minor.
  * The qualify_requested event and the qualify spool: a plugin with no
    verdict added under require_pins with pin_mode first-use says
    qualify_requested with its uri, and one request for its quick
    qualification is written in the spool (#107).
  * The qualification_dir conf key, its OMX_QUALIFICATION_DIR default and the
    subdirectory constant are dropped: plugin-hostd reads qualifications
    through libplugin-qualification-db, so the key has no reader (#112).
  * The plugin-db words of the rendered vocabulary come from plugin-db 0.4.7's
    domain (#111); the plugin-db-contract floor stays 0.4.4.
  * The table-constants check joins verb_table.py (#108).
  * The Debian packages build on arm64 runners and Fedora 45 is the newest
    cell, Fedora 44 dropped; the ABI baseline carries the types, not only
    the symbols (#113).
  * The commit identity check is on for pull requests (#115).
  * The Breaks and Replaces of the ca language pack against plugin-hostd-
    protocol-contract (<< 0.5.6) are gone: floors only, no Breaks, Replaces
    or Conflicts between our packages.
  * The soname stays libplugin-hostd-protocol.so.0: the exported symbols and
    the layout of every type are as in 0.6.0, the removed names were
    enumerators and macros that a consumer resolves when it compiles.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Floors only, no ceilings, declared once in packaging/deps.txt; the spec
    and debian/control are generated from it and the floors check refuses
    drift (#64): omx-dsp-devel >= 0.32.4 (0.5.9 declared 0.32.1), omx-
    contract 3.19.1 (0.5.9 declared 3.18.0: the release the headers are
    rendered with), and plugin-db 0.4.4 as before.
  * python3-plugin-hostd-client, a new noarch package: the protocol's Python
    client ships from here (#47, #45).
  * python3-plugin-hostd-protocol, the Python codec, ships from here (#48,
    #46).
  * The grammar's quoted-escaped form, a quoted value that is text, for the
    property verbs (#39).
  * The panel file declares its keys, meters among them (#51).
  * The typed replies have a JSON Schema each, installed under shapesdir,
    and the TypeScript render is published as an npm package (#82, #81); the
    TypeScript client of the protocol, its transport, the generated
    vocabulary and curvePoints, ships in the same package (#87).
  * The protocol schemas take https://openmixer.org/schema/plugin-hostd-
    protocol/ as their $id (#99).
  * An untagged empty line, and a whitespace-only one, gets no reply and
    changes no state; a tagged one keeps its answer (#79, #83).
  * phd_note_valid reads no word past count, phd_pin_path_decode writes
    nothing into a size of 0 (#74), and phd_number_in reads one spelling per
    number, in the caller's lo and hi only (#75).
  * The command and feedback markers of mod-host.h that the generator reads
    are back (#80).
  * The installed C headers document their public API with Doxygen, and the
    documentation gates only shrink (#62, #69, #76, #78).
  * The curve families of omx-dsp 0.32.4: the delay and reverb curve
    families and the 37 roles curve_bind takes, with time_response, which a
    curve verb draws as omx-dsp does (#93).
  * rpc_timeout_ms: a silent worker gets SIGTERM first, so it closes its
    JACK client, and SIGKILL only if it has not left two seconds later
    (#89).
  * No epoch on any package of this source (#95, #97).
  * CI: the heavy workflows run by dispatch and tags, the fast checks alone
    on a pull request (#43); each cell takes its cells from check-matrix
    (#37).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.5.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Built against plugin-db >= 0.4.4 and below 0.5 and omx-dsp >= 0.32.1 and
    below 0.33, the 3.18.0 pass's newest of each, with their ceilings (D30).
  * CI renders against what the channel serves every day, the render check
    alone, and names the served contract packages when it fails (#27, #32).
  * The fuzz seed corpus is held to its generator on every pull request, and
    the generator writes the same corpus in every locale (LC_ALL=C); the
    corpus and both golden transcripts are written again over it (#33, #34).
  * The default CLAP search path holds the folders distributions install
    plugins in, /usr/local/lib/clap, /usr/lib64/clap and /usr/local/lib64/clap,
    after clap/entry.h's: a fresh plugin-hostd learns a first-use pin there
    (plugin-hostd#82, #36).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

